    "# Quiz: K-Means clustering\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-2-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>K-Means is derived from:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>electrical engineering</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. K-Means comes from the domain of signal processing.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>signal processing</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. K-Means is a method derived from the domain of signal processing.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>computational linguistics</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. K-Means was derived from signal processing.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-2-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>A good Silhouette score means:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>clusters are well-separated and well-defined</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. A score near 1 means the clusters are dense and well-separated from other clusters.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>there are few clusters</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The silhouette score is about how dense and well-separated clusters are. A score near 1 is good.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>there are many clusters</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A good silhouette score is close to 1, meaning the clusters are dense and well-separated.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-2-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Variance is:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>the average of the squared differences from the mean</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. That is the definition, but too much variance also made the song data hard to cluster. Both are true.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a problem for clustering if it becomes too high</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. That is true, but variance is also defined as the average of the squared differences from the mean.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>both of these</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Variance is the average of the squared differences from the mean, and too much of it made the song data hard to cluster.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-2-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>A Voronoi diagram shows:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a cluster's variance</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A Voronoi diagram shows a point, or 'seed', and its region for each cluster.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a cluster's seed and its region</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. A Voronoi diagram shows each cluster as a point, or 'seed', and its region.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a cluster's inertia</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A Voronoi diagram pictures the clusters: each has a point, or 'seed', and its region.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-2-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Inertia is</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a measure of how internally coherent clusters are</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Inertia measures how internally coherent clusters are: how close each cluster's points are to its center.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a measure of how much clusters move</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Inertia is not about movement. It measures how close the points in each cluster are to its center.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a measure of cluster quality</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Inertia measures one specific thing: how internally coherent clusters are, or how close points are to their center.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-5-2-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Using K-Means, you must first determine the value of 'k'</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>true</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. With K-Means you must set 'k', the number of centroids. The elbow method helps pick a good value.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>false</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. You need to set 'k', the number of centroids, before K-Means runs. This is one of its drawbacks.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
